# Nodepad Architecture & Coding Guidelines

## 1. State Management (Zustand)
- **Rule**: All persistent or global state must reside in `lib/store.ts` using Zustand.
- **Why**: Prevents prop drilling and keeps components like `page.tsx` clean.

## 2. AI & Async Logic (Hooks)
- **Rule**: Do not put heavy `fetch` or AI generation logic directly in components. Use dedicated custom hooks like `lib/hooks/useNodepadAI.ts`.
- **Why**: Separates business logic from UI, making it easier to swap AI providers later.

## 3. i18n (Internationalization)
- **Rule**: Never hardcode UI text (Korean or English) in components. Always use the `useTranslation` hook from `lib/i18n.ts`.
- **Why**: Enables easy addition of new languages in the future without touching component code.

## 4. Theming & Styling (CSS Variables)
- **Rule**: Do not hardcode specific border-radius or complex shadows. Use CSS variables defined in `app/globals.css` (e.g. `var(--radius)`).
- **Why**: Allows swapping the entire app's look and feel by changing `data-theme` on the body.

Follow these rules rigidly during any code modification or refactoring.
